%% PL3 p.14 + P1 p.2: instance 2 fails - its data stays readable from the copies, circuit breaker, automatic recovery
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant I1 as instance1 (copy of F)
    participant I2 as instance2 (owner of F)

    Note over I2: instance 2 goes down
    C->>I1: GET flight F (owned by instance 2)
    Note over I1: F is in instance 1's own database (copy)
    I1-->>C: 200 F, X-Data-Source: local (no outage for the client)
    C->>I1: GET flights of an aircraft (list)
    I1-xI2: attempt 1: connection refused
    Note over I1: wait ~100 ms, then ~200 ms
    I1-xI2: attempts 2 and 3 - 3 failures in a row: circuit OPEN (10 s)
    I1-->>C: 200 complete list, X-Unreachable-Peers: 1 (every flight has a running copy)
    C->>I1: POST booking for an aircraft owned by instance 2
    Note over I1: circuit open: instance 2 skipped (fail fast)<br/>instance 1 is the aircraft's backup - booked here
    Note over I1: outbox: "send flight G to instance 2" (same transaction)
    I1-->>C: 201 G, X-Stored-On: instance1
    Note over I2: instance 2 restarts (even with an empty database)
    I2->>I1: catch-up: GET /internal/replicas?for=instance2
    I1-->>I2: its flights, incl. G - applied before instance 2 reports ready
    I1->>I2: health check GET /actuator/health (every 5 s)
    I2-->>I1: 200 UP - circuit CLOSED
    I1->>I2: outbox: POST /internal/replicas G (already there: no change) - task deleted
